{{!--
  The marketing top nav.

  For a signed-in visitor the right-hand slot is the ACCOUNT MENU: the
  user's name, and a dropdown holding the four things an account owner
  reaches for — 个人中心 (the console), 档案 (the profile details),
  更改密码 (the password form) and 注销 (log out).

  Two decisions worth stating:

  1. It is a <details> element, not a JS-driven dropdown. The page's
     CSP is `script-src 'self'`, so an inline handler is blocked, and an
     external controller would have to re-implement focus management,
     Escape handling and outside-click dismissal that <details> gives
     for free. <details> also works with no JavaScript at all, which
     means the menu still opens if the asset fails to load.

  2. 注销 is a POST, not a link. Logging out mutates server state, so
     it carries a CSRF token; a GET link would be forgeable by any
     <img src="/logout"> on a third-party page.

  3. No `role="menu"`. The ARIA menu widget obliges the author to move
     focus between items with the arrow keys. There is no key handler
     for this menu — the page's CSP forbids inline scripts and no
     controller exists for it — so claiming the role would promise an
     interaction that is not there. A list of links inside a disclosure
     needs no role at all, and keeps the browser's native Tab
     navigation, which is what a keyboard user expects of a list of
     links anyway.

  The name shown is the display name when the account has one, and the
  email address otherwise — an account with no nickname still has to be
  identifiable in the header.
--}}
<nav class="m-topnav">
  <div class="m-topnav-inner">
    <a href="/" class="m-topnav-brand">
      <span class="m-topnav-brand-mark">ip</span>
      IPQuery
    </a>
    <div class="m-topnav-links">
      <a href="/docs" class="{{#if isDocs}}active{{/if}}">{{req.t 'nav.docs'}}</a>
      <a href="/try" class="{{#if isTry}}active{{/if}}">{{req.t 'nav.try'}}</a>
      <a href="/status" class="{{#if isStatus}}active{{/if}}">{{req.t 'nav.status'}}</a>
      <a href="/about" class="{{#if isAbout}}active{{/if}}">{{req.t 'nav.about'}}</a>
    </div>
    <div class="m-topnav-cta">
      {{#if req.user}}
        <details class="m-account">
          <summary class="m-account-trigger" aria-label="{{req.t 'nav.account'}}">
            <span class="m-account-avatar" aria-hidden="true">{{accountInitial}}</span>
            <span class="m-account-name">{{accountLabel}}</span>
            <svg class="m-account-caret" width="10" height="6" viewBox="0 0 10 6" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
              <path d="M1 1l4 4 4-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
            </svg>
          </summary>
          <div class="m-account-menu">
            <a class="m-account-item" href="/dashboard">{{req.t 'nav.account'}}</a>
            <a class="m-account-item" href="/dashboard/profile/details">{{req.t 'nav.profileDetails'}}</a>
            <a class="m-account-item" href="/dashboard/profile/password">{{req.t 'nav.changePassword'}}</a>
            <form method="POST" action="/logout" class="m-account-form">
              <input type="hidden" name="csrf" value="{{req.csrfToken}}">
              <button type="submit" class="m-account-item m-account-item-danger">{{req.t 'nav.logout'}}</button>
            </form>
          </div>
        </details>
      {{else}}
        <a href="/login" class="m-text-link">{{req.t 'nav.login'}}</a>
        <a href="/signup" class="button button-small">{{req.t 'common.signup'}}</a>
      {{/if}}
    </div>
  </div>
</nav>
